# Picks ONE field out of an index line and undoes the escaping that
# $indexClean put in. Returns the empty string when the field is not there,
# which is also the honest answer for a field that is there and empty.
#
# Fields are name=value joined by tab. The search starts AT a tab, so a field
# name can never be matched inside a value. The first field carries no leading
# tab of its own, hence the one that is put in front here.
#
# This is the mirror of $indexClean and the only other place that knows the
# encoding. If the escaping ever grows a scanner, these two move together.

If len(pEntry)=0
	Quit method ''
End If
Calculate text as con(kTab,pEntry)
Calculate text2 as con(kTab,pFieldName,'=')
Calculate n as pos(text2,text)
If n=0
	Quit method ''
End If
Calculate n as n+len(text2)
Calculate text as mid(text,n,len(text)-n+1)
Calculate n as pos(kTab,text)
If n>0
	Calculate text as mid(text,1,n-1)
End If
Calculate text as replaceall(text,'\t',kTab)
Calculate text as replaceall(text,'\n',kCr)
Quit method text